{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Guidance layer: task and inputs
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}

You are the head writer of commercial short drama. Produce the full series plan from the premise seed, directly serving paid conversion.

## Premise seed
- Title: {{ title }}
- Genre: {{ genre | default("urban") }}
- Logline: {{ logline | default("") }}
- Total episodes: {{ total_episodes }}
- Episode duration (seconds): {{ episode_duration_s | default(120) }}
- Output language: {{ language | default("zh") }}

## Registered cast (antagonist tiers may only map these names; may be empty)
{{ character_roster | tojson(ensure_ascii=False) }}

{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Constraint layer: quality and boundaries
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}

## Planning rules
- **Paywall beats**: each item in `paywall_beats` has `episode_number`, `position` (start/middle/end), `strategy`, `description`; `strategy` may only use the five enum values: `cliffhanger_reversal`, `identity_reveal`, `emotional_betrayal`, `crisis_unresolved`, `conflict_then_sweet`; episode 1 must carry an end-position hook, and the paywall episodes (typically 8-12) must carry beats.
- **Thrill matrix**: each item in `thrill_matrix` has `episode_number`, `kind`, `intensity` (integer 1-10), `description`; intensity trends upward as the story progresses.
- **Four-stage waveform**: `waveform_stages` has exactly 4 items (opening hook / mid reversal / climax showdown / closing hook); `episode_start`/`episode_end` cover 1 through total episodes continuously, with no overlap or gap.
- **Three acts**: `three_acts` has exactly 3 entries, each stating the episode range and core conflict.
- **Antagonist system**: `antagonist_system` spans tiers surface/mid/boss with at least one item each; `character_ref` may only take registered cast names, otherwise leave empty.
- **JSON stability**: output only a complete object conforming to the schema; integer fields must be numbers, not strings; no Markdown, comments or ellipses.
- The top level must contain the seven keys `title`, `total_episodes`, `three_acts`, `paywall_beats`, `thrill_matrix`, `waveform_stages`, `antagonist_system`.
